d Federation with Identity Providers.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-03-17\nValid as Of: 2025-03-20\nVersion: 2502b\n\n--- Record 1187 ---\nComponent: Cloud Portal Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Identity Authentication is the Default Authentication Mechanism for New Subscriptions\nDescription: For new subscriptions to SAP Cloud Portal service, the default authentication method is now Identity Authentication. Existing subscriptions will not be affected  Make sure that you have an OIDC-based trust between SAP Cloud Identity Services – Identity Authentication and SAP BTP.   For more information, see Establish Trust and Federation Between SAP Authorization and Trust Management Service and SAP Cloud Identity Services.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-03-13\nValid as Of: 2025-03-20\nVersion: 2502B\n\n--- Record 1188 ---\nComponent: Connectivity\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Destination Service - New Features\nDescription:   The Destination service REST API now allows to use an additional header to indicate that a specified fragment for the call is optional and the API should succeed and return the destination \"\"as is\"\" in case there is no fragment with the specified name.  Added a new filter when making \"\"get all\"\" calls to the REST API of the service, which allows to look up only the entities created or updated during the last n minutes. Where n is a value specified by the caller. The upper limit for n is 1 day.  You can now instruct the service to include certain metadata properties of the entity in the service response when making \"\"get all\"\" calls to the REST API.  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-03-20\nValid as Of: 2025-03-20\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1189 ---\nComponent: Custom Domain Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Sending Configuration Data to SAP Cloud ALM\nDescription: To fulfill security requirements, Custom Domain Manager now sends user configurations in a standardised format to SAP Cloud ALM. For more information, see Configuration & Security Analysis.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-03-20\nValid as Of: 2025-03-20\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1190 ---\nComponent: Data Quality Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Neo\nTitle: Enhancements\nDescription:   The microservice generates a new address information code 5510 when an address is selected from type ahead suggestions that is not in the postal authority reference data. See Information Codes for Address Cleanse form more information.   The microservice added a new geoAssign setting to the Reverse Geocoding endpoint. This setting offers control for the endpoint to return only full addresses, or results representing a street or a city when the reference data does not have full addresses for the location. See Reverse Geocoding Settings for more information.   \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-01\nValid as Of: 2025-03-20\nVersion: Cloud\n\n\",147\n\n\nOutput:\n", "role": "user"}], "parameters": {"model": "gpt-4o", "frequency_penalty": 0.0, "max_tokens": null, "n": 1, "presence_penalty": 0.0, "temperature": 0.0, "top_p": 1.0, "response_format": {"type": "json_object"}}}, "key": "chat_create_community_report_4c015491eaa98ad27a4c679402e6f425f43fe648561ecf263247a0693da2c219_v2"}